{"content_id":"CL-AUD-HR08-NOISE-001","domain_id_primary":"D-AUD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-audio-02-live-systems.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-audio.mjs","course_id":"C-AUD-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"3","lesson_identifier":"3.2","block_identifier":"hearing-safety","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Under OSHA 29 CFR 1910.95 where applicable, 85 dBA as an 8-hour TWA is the hearing-conservation action level, while Table G-16 lists 90 dBA for 8 hours as a permissible-exposure point in OSHA's general-industry framework.","content_classification":"external_fact","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"This normalized claim corrects the learner-facing wording without treating either threshold as a universal safe/unsafe boundary."}
{"content_id":"CL-AUD-HR08-NOISE-002","domain_id_primary":"D-AUD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"boundary","route_file":"courses/pathway-audio-02-live-systems.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-audio.mjs","course_id":"C-AUD-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"3","lesson_identifier":"3.2","block_identifier":"hearing-safety-wording","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Do not describe OSHA's 5-dB exchange relationship as a universal 'safe exposure time' rule; it belongs to OSHA's specific occupational-noise framework and employer monitoring/protection duties.","content_classification":"safety_boundary","safety_criticality":"high","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"draft_only","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Current learner text should be revised before stronger release."}
{"content_id":"CL-AUD-HR08-WIRELESS-001","domain_id_primary":"D-AUD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-RF"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-audio-02-live-systems.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-audio.mjs","course_id":"C-AUD-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"3","lesson_identifier":"3.2","block_identifier":"wireless-domains","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A wireless audio path contains an RF transport domain and a downstream audio domain; a working RF link does not by itself prove the receiver output and downstream console/audio path are correct.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Troubleshooting framework only; no frequency-coordination procedure is taught."}
{"content_id":"CL-AUD-HR08-DANTE-001","domain_id_primary":"D-AUD","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-audio-02-live-systems.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-audio.mjs","course_id":"C-AUD-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"3","lesson_identifier":"3.2","block_identifier":"networked-audio","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Dante is an audio/AV-over-IP ecosystem in which logical routing, device/network state and clocking can affect whether a physically connected system passes audio correctly.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"system_reasoning","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"High-level awareness only; no independent Dante-network configuration authority is implied."}
{"content_id":"CL-AUD-HR08-DANTE-BOUNDARY-001","domain_id_primary":"D-AUD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"boundary","route_file":"courses/pathway-audio-02-live-systems.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-audio.mjs","course_id":"C-AUD-SYSTEMS","tier_learning":"T4","responsibility_band":"R2","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"3","lesson_identifier":"3.2","block_identifier":"network-boundary","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Course 2 networked-audio awareness does not authorize independent IP addressing, VLAN design, multicast architecture, switch configuration or Dante network engineering.","content_classification":"safety_boundary","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"specialist_external","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Product/network-specific configuration remains employer/vendor/practitioner controlled."}
{"content_id":"CL-AUD-HR08-RF-C3-001","domain_id_primary":"D-AUD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-RF"],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-audio-03-system-design.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-advanced.mjs","course_id":"C-AUD-SYSTEM-DESIGN","tier_learning":"T7","responsibility_band":"R5","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Acoustics, Networks & RF","lesson_identifier":"Coordinate Three Specialist Domains","block_identifier":"rf-view","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Professional wireless-audio work can include RF inventory, spectrum scanning, frequency coordination, deployment-state management and ongoing monitoring; these functions form a specialist RF domain separate from basic audio signal-flow literacy.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"specialist_external","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Descriptive role architecture only. No frequencies, coordination calculations or operational RF procedure are taught by this matrix claim."}
{"content_id":"CL-AUD-HR08-RF-REG-001","domain_id_primary":"D-AUD","domain_ids_secondary":["D-RF"],"content_type":"boundary","route_file":"courses/pathway-audio-03-system-design.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-advanced.mjs","course_id":"C-AUD-SYSTEM-DESIGN","tier_learning":"T7","responsibility_band":"R5","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Acoustics, Networks & RF","lesson_identifier":"Coordinate Three Specialist Domains","block_identifier":"rf-regulatory-boundary","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Wireless-microphone operation exists within an evolving FCC spectrum/rules environment; Crew Blueprint system-architecture study does not substitute for current regulatory, product, venue or experienced RF-coordination review.","content_classification":"safety_boundary","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"specialist_external","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"No operational frequency guidance is provided here."}
{"content_id":"CL-AUD-HR08-NET-C3-001","domain_id_primary":"D-AUD","domain_ids_secondary":[],"content_type":"claim","route_file":"courses/pathway-audio-03-system-design.html","source_data_file":"scripts/course-data-advanced.mjs","course_id":"C-AUD-SYSTEM-DESIGN","tier_learning":"T7","responsibility_band":"R5","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"Acoustics, Networks & RF","lesson_identifier":"Coordinate Three Specialist Domains","block_identifier":"network-view","question_identifier":null,"visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Advanced audio-system architecture may need to account for physical versus logical topology, device discovery/routing, clock state, multicast behavior, segmentation and redundancy, but the exact network design belongs to qualified product/network practitioners.","content_classification":"cross_source_pattern","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"specialist_external","publication_state":"noindex_review","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Vendor/platform evidence supports these as real concerns; not all are universal protocol mandates in every Dante system."}
